    "title": "Firepower to Invincible Shield: Six Years, the Same Rig",
    "content": "The story from *Firepower* (2018) to *Invincible Shield* (2024) spans six years on the same long-standing endorsement lineup. Scott Travis has been a long-time endorser of ddrum, Paiste Cymbals, DW Pedals, and Vic Firth Drumsticks with no documented brand changes across his Priest career, and *Invincible Shield* is no exception.\n\n**Drums:**\nThe ddrum Dominion Series shell pack that anchored *Firepower* carried over unchanged for *Invincible Shield*. The bass drum dimensions (22\"x18\", x2 independent) also carried over unchanged.\n\n**Snare:**\nThe ddrum Scott Travis Signature 14\"x6.5\" is the same snare Travis has used since *Painkiller*, including on both *Firepower* and *Invincible Shield*.\n\n**Cymbals:**\nTravis's Paiste RUDE/2002 cymbal voice, which has anchored his sound since *Painkiller*, carried through *Firepower* and into *Invincible Shield* unchanged.\n\n**Hardware:**\nThe DW 9000 Series double pedal Travis has used since *Painkiller* remained his choice for *Invincible Shield*. Travis's fundamental approach — two independent pedals, no connected double pedal — has not changed since 1990.\n\n**What Didn't Change:**\nVic Firth's American Classic 5B stick model carried through unchanged, as did the Evans head package and the tight, medium-high snare tuning philosophy documented on every Priest album since *Painkiller*. Six years, and the fundamentals — precision, articulation, and a rig Travis has trusted for decades — did not move.",
